Package: tabfound
Title: Tabular Foundation Models in Pure R Torch
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Marcel", "Neunhoeffer",
           email = "marcel@marcel-neunhoeffer.com",
           role  = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Inference-only R implementations of open-weight tabular
    foundation models on top of the 'torch' package, with no Python
    runtime dependency at predict time. A backend registry lets a single
    user-facing API ('tabular_classifier()' / 'tabular_regressor()')
    serve architecturally different models. Ships a TabPFN v2 backend
    (Prior-Labs) verified bit-exact against the reference Python
    implementation, and shared building blocks (attention variants,
    RMSNorm, RoPE, set-transformer blocks, quantile/power/SVD
    preprocessing, ensembling) for adding further backends such as
    Google's TabFM and TabICL.
